    {
      "id": 234724,
      "name": "der andere Jan",
      "username": "der_andere_Jan",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/{size}/1881_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-01-17T14:47:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'd say don't get too mechanic, and just go with what works for the story.</p>\n<p>If you want them to get some information easily, let them bump into someone who turns out a bug fan, and who just so happens to work for the Mayor. If you want them to be stuck, or work especially hard, all their allies&nbsp;are out of town (you can even drop a running gag when it slowly becomes clear they are all visiting the same obscure butterfly breeders convention everybody knows about, except of course the heroes).</p>\n<p>It's comic, so any cheesy reasoning usually works better than realistic probabilities.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:10:53.335Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
